COMM 39K(p,gamma)40Ca 1-gamma cascade, script-generated dense-grid
COMM point (generate_reactions.py) -- terminus: fictional single-gamma terminus at 8.5500 MeV excitation, e_budget =
COMM 8.55000 MeV. Every level is a FICTIONAL placeholder, unused by
COMM kinematics beyond fixing gamma energies (see ReactionConfig.hh's own LEVL
COMM comment) -- same convention as every hand-written file in this directory.
COMM Single-gamma calibration source, RECL(e_budget=8.55000)=-34.4622.
COMM Levels (excitation above terminus, MeV): (none -- single gamma)
COMM Gamma energies before recoil-kinematics corrections (MeV): gamma1=8.5500
COMM Verify with `--reaction-stats <this file>`.

BEAM 19  39   -33.8072     # Z A massExcessMeV -- 39K
TARG 1   1    7.28897      # 1H (target, at rest)
RECL 20  40   -34.462230000000005  8  # 40Ca -- fictional single-gamma terminus at 8.5500 MeV excitation
ERES 0.606                  # CM resonance energy above threshold, MeV


BRAT   -1  100.0   0        # resonance -> terminus directly, 100%, single gamma
SENT
